# p_c3d4 — Yuki works from the office desk three days a week

Yuki has a dedicated office (desk_o1, office_chair_o1, office_shelf_o1) and works from it on Monday, Wednesday, and Friday from 08:00 to 17:30. On Tuesday and Thursday she cycles to the office in town. Her laptop, notebook, and pen are at desk_o1 during WFH days and travel with her on commute days. Omar follows the same cycling pattern as the standard model. This hypothesis is distinguished by the laptop and notebook being at desk_o1 (not the entry or OUT_OF_HOUSE) on Mon/Wed/Fri between 08:00 and 17:30. What would refute it: finding Yuki's laptop at the entry hook or OUT_OF_HOUSE on a Monday between 09:00 and 16:00, or finding it at desk_o1 on a Tuesday at noon.

```json
{
 "claims": [
  {
   "claim": "Yuki's laptop is at the office desk on Monday mornings",
   "target": "laptop_yuki",
   "expect": "desk_o1",
   "days": "weekday",
   "from": 9,
   "to": 16
  },
  {
   "claim": "Yuki's notebook is at the office desk on Wednesday afternoons",
   "target": "notebook_yuki",
   "expect": "desk_o1",
   "days": "weekday",
   "from": 10,
   "to": 16
