# p_4e91 — Both drive on weekdays; cycling is a weekend-morning ritual

Neither Yuki nor Omar cycles on weekdays. Yuki drives to her office (8:00–17:30) and Omar drives to his afternoon shift (13:40–23:00). Their bikes, helmets, and bike locks stay at the entry all week. On weekends both sleep in until about 9:00, then go cycling together 10:00–13:00, taking helmets, bike locks, water bottles, and jackets out. After cycling they run errands until about 14:30. Yuki's laptop, notebook, pen, keys, and wallet go OUT_OF_HOUSE on weekdays 8:00–17:30. Omar's tablet stays in chair_k1 (it is a home entertainment device, not a work tool). What sets this apart: no cycling gear is ever out on a weekday, and the weekend 10:00–13:00 window is the only cycling window. What would refute it: helmet_yuki or bike_lock_omar sighted OUT_OF_HOUSE on a weekday, or both helmets in the house on a Saturday morning between 10:00 and 13:00.

